<h2 class="font-headline-md text-headline-md text-on-surface">Problem Description</h2>
</div>
<div class="p-space-md bg-surface-container-low rounded-lg text-on-surface font-body-md text-body-md leading-relaxed">
<p class="mb-space-sm">
<strong class="font-semibold text-primary">Centralized traffic forecasting</strong> requires edge cameras and roadside sensors to continuously stream raw telemetry and video vectors to a central cloud, consuming vast cellular bandwidth and concentrating private travel logs in a singular point of failure.
            </p>
<p>
<strong class="font-semibold text-secondary">Federated Learning (FL)</strong> addresses this vulnerability by orchestrating on-device training across local edge intersection nodes and transmitting only mathematical parameter weight updates (<code class="font-mono text-label-sm bg-surface-container px-1 py-0.5 rounded">Δw</code>) to an aggregation server. In this research problem, participants construct a federated simulator over a partitioned real-world traffic repository, comparing a compact architecture (e.g., GRU, STGCN, LSTM) running FedAvg against centralized baselines across Non-IID skew conditions while rigorously tracking transmitted network byte footprints.
            </p>
</div>
<!-- Paradigm Comparison: Centralized vs Federated -->
<div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-space-md mt-space-xs">
<!-- Centralized Inefficiencies -->
<div class="bg-surface-container-lowest p-space-md rounded-lg flex flex-col gap-space-xs border border-error/20">
<div class="flex items-center gap-space-xs text-error font-headline-sm text-headline-sm">
<span class="material-symbols-outlined text-[20px]">cloud_sync</span>
<span>Centralized Paradigm</span>
</div>
<ul class="flex flex-col gap-space-xs font-body-sm text-body-sm text-on-surface-variant mt-space-xs list-disc list-inside">
<li><span class="text-on-surface font-medium">Raw Streaming:</span> Unbounded multi-gigabyte telemetry ingress to central servers.</li>
<li><span class="text-on-surface font-medium">Privacy Exposure:</span> High-resolution license plate trajectories and vehicle spatio-temporal logs stored centrally.</li>
<li><span class="text-on-surface font-medium">Bandwidth Tax:</span> Massive ongoing 4G/5G cellular overhead prone to link congestion and latency spikes.</li>
</ul>
</div>
<!-- Federated Optimization -->
<div class="bg-surface-container-lowest p-space-md rounded-lg flex flex-col gap-space-xs border border-on-tertiary-container/20">
<div class="flex items-center gap-space-xs text-on-tertiary-container font-headline-sm text-headline-sm">
<span class="material-symbols-outlined text-[20px]">share</span>
<span>Federated Paradigm (FedAvg)</span>
</div>
<ul class="flex flex-col gap-space-xs font-body-sm text-body-sm text-on-surface-variant mt-space-xs list-disc list-inside">
<li><span class="text-on-surface font-medium">Edge Compute:</span> Local training on roadside processing units (RSUs) or intersection edge controllers.</li>
<li><span class="text-on-surface font-medium">Privacy Preservation:</span> Raw vehicle count time-series never leaves the local node boundary.</li>
<li><span class="text-on-surface font-medium">Quantized Payloads:</span> Periodic transmission restricted strictly to model weights per communication round.</li>
</ul>
</div>
</div>
